        "original_id": "4ae20f93-99a8-55bb-bb0b-31efdec49f47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ken Kwapis, John Woo\n- Roles: film director, television director, screenwriter\n- Works: Sesame Street Presents Follow That Bird, The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants, He's Just Not That into You, Vibes, A Better Tomorrow, The Killer, Hard Boiled, Red Cliff\n- Topics: single-camera sitcoms\n\nFacts:\n- Ken Kwapis was born on August 17, 1957, and he is an American film and television director and screenwriter.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the feature film \"Sesame Street Presents Follow That Bird\" in 1985.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the film \"Vibes.\"\n- John Woo directed the Hong Kong action film \"A Better Tomorrow\" in 1986.\n- John Woo directed the Hong Kong action film \"The Killer\" in 1989.\n- Ken Kwapis specialized in the single-camera sitcom in the 1990s and 2000s.\n- John Woo directed the Hong Kong action film \"Hard Boiled\" in 1992.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the feature film \"The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants\" in 2005.\n- John Woo directed \"Red Cliff\" in 2008 and 2009.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the feature film \"He's Just Not That into You\" in 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "29377c3b-3cc1-5203-9097-b36a945d40e7",
        "text": "Page: Ken Kwapis. Sentence: Kenneth William \"Ken\" Kwapis (born August 17, 1957) is an American film and television director and screenwriter.\nPage: Ken Kwapis. Sentence: He specialized in the single-camera sitcom in the 1990s and 2000s and has directed feature films such as \"Sesame Street Presents Follow That Bird\" (1985), \"The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants\" (2005), and \"He's Just Not That into You\" (2009).\nPage: John Woo. Sentence: Woo has directed several notable Hong Kong action films, among them, \"A Better Tomorrow\" (1986), \"The Killer\" (1989), \"Hard Boiled\" (1992), and \"Red Cliff\" (2008/2009).\nPage: Vibes (film). Sentence: It was directed by Ken Kwapis.",
